  "description_damage": "The brown wheat mite is tiny, dark, and less than 0.03 inch in length, with front legs longer than the body. Feeding mottles the leaves, giving them a bronzed, silvery, or (later) scorched appearance. Host plants include cereals, onions, carrots, alfalfa, iris, and gladiolus.",
